            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court must decide the scope of Congress\u2019s power to impose registration requirements on individuals convicted of federal crimes, including sex offenses, after they have completed their sentences."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Fifth Circuit previously held that Congress\u2019s authority ends once the individual completes his criminal sentence."
      }
    ],
