          },
          {
            "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States argues that Congress has authority under the Necessary and Proper Clause to impose civil registration requirements on federal sex offenders as a means of protecting public safety."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, convicted sex offenders pose a serious threat to public safety, justifying such federal sanctions."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, congress may impose both criminal and civil sanctions for federal sex offender convictions to protect the public."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 10,
                "start": 10
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, the authority to impose such requirements is grounded in the Necessary and Proper Clause."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, the situation differs from the Comstock case because the federal government is not the source of the problem in incarcerating sex offenders away from the states."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Fuentes",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Fuentes, sORNA illustrates how registration works today and supports the United States\u2019 position."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Fuentes",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "bcf1e11cd0e8876e4b2c5d1df5ac02c370f72e8d42c343045d35f20067c846cf",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-bcf1e11cd0e8-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Fuentes, registration can be imposed only if the provision was part of the sentence or while the individual remained under federal jurisdiction."
        }
      ],
